183347	183402	183319	183319	his	8022	“ DEAR SIR -- When you did me the favor of calling here a few days since , you asked a question relating to my governess , Miss Gwilt , which I thought rather a strange one at the time , and which caused , as you may remember , a momentary embarrassment between us .
183403	183523	183319	183319	his	8022	“ This morning the subject of Miss Gwilt has been brought to my notice again in a manner which has caused me the utmost astonishment . In plain words , Mrs. Milroy has informed me that Miss Gwilt has exposed herself to the suspicion of having deceived us by a false reference . On my expressing the surprise which such an extraordinary statement caused me , and requesting that it might be instantly substantiated , I was still further astonished by being told to apply for all particulars to no less a person than Mr. Armadale . I have vainly requested some further explanation from Mrs. Milroy ; she persists in maintaining silence , and in referring me to yourself .
183524	183580	183319	183319	his	8022	“ Under these extraordinary circumstances , I am compelled , in justice to all parties , to ask you certain questions which I will endeavor to put as plainly as possible , and which I am quite ready to believe ( from my previous experience of you ) that you will answer frankly on your side .
