339127	339302	339110	339111	the doctor	486	“ are , as you have seen , in a partially unfinished condition . Under any circumstances , I should lay little stress on the grounds , having Hampstead Heath so near at hand , and carriage exercise and horse exercise being parts of my System . In a lesser degree , it is also necessary for me to ask your indulgence for the basement floor , on which we now stand . The waiting - room and study on that side , and the Dispensary on the other ( to which I shall presently ask your attention ) , are completed . But the large drawing - room is still in the decorator ’s hands . In that room ( when the walls are dry -- not a moment before ) my inmates will assemble for cheerful society . Nothing will be spared that can improve , elevate , and adorn life at these happy little gatherings . Every evening , for example , there will be music for those who like it . ”
